From: denfry <dabinayo@pm.me>
Date: Fri, 30 Oct 2026 11:02:15 +0300
Subject: [PATCH] Track waypoints across regions for the locator bar

Folia left the waypoint manager empty, so the locator bar never showed
anything. Keep the waypoints and receiving players of a world in
concurrent sets and let every receiver poll them on its own thread each
tick: it connects, updates and drops its connections the same way the
vanilla manager does when a waypoint or the player moves. Connections
live on the receiving player, so no shared table is touched from
several regions. A changed icon bumps the waypoint version, which makes
receivers remake the connection; turning the locator bar off drops the
connections on the receivers' next tick.

